{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UXmgBxjrsdraqWCMs53A13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario. Let me look at which experiments are still planned/running/queued (not DONE):\n\nFrom the registry, the experiments that are QUEUED or RUNNING (i.e., pending):\n1. `exception_only_nomarker_seed42` - QUEUED\n2. `loop_only_seed123` - RUNNING\n3. `loop_only_seed456` - QUEUED\n4. `exception_only_nomarker_seed123` - QUEUED\n\n\n5. `exception_only_nomarker_seed456` - QUEUED\n6. `qwen15b_vota_seed42` - RUNNING\n7. `qwen15b_full_trace_seed42` - QUEUED\n8. `codellama13b_exception_only_seed42` - QUEUED\n9. `codellama13b_no_trace_seed42` - QUEUED\n10. `codellama13b_vota_seed42` - QUEUED\n\nI also need to account for the killed experiments like `qwen1.5b_exception_only_seed42` and `qwen1.5b_no_trace_seed42` when compiling the full list.\n\nLooking at the newer versions, I see `qwen15b_no_trace_seed42` finished with 0.6731 accuracy and `qwen15b_exception_only_seed42` achieved 0.9983 accuracy, while `qwen15b_vota_seed42` is still running. The remaining pending experiments that still need predictions include `exception_only_nomarker_seed42`, `loop_only_seed123`, and a few others that are either queued or running.\n\nFrom the performance data, it looks like the smaller Qwen-1.5B model's VOTA approach performs comparably to exception-only tracing on these tasks, suggesting that VOTA isn't losing much on smaller models. Looking at the performance metrics across these experiments, I'm seeing that Qwen-1.5B with VOTA achieves 99.0-99.83% accuracy, which contradicts the hypothesis that small models hit execution bottlenecks with VOTA traces. The variance patterns show loop_only configurations are unstable across seeds, while the effective model count has dropped to just 2 viable candidates. I'm shifting the narrative away from exception dominance toward a minimal representation hypothesis — that diagnostic signals alone might be sufficient without full exception traces. contradicting the \"execution reasoning bottleneck\" hypothesis. I'll predict ~99.5%.\n\n2. **qwen15b_full_trace_seed42** (QUEUED): Full trace on 1.5B should struggle more than the 7B version (81.76%), so I'm estimating around 72-78% given the reduced model capacity.\n\n3. **loop_only_seed123** (RUNNING): This one's dropping to around 79-80%, compared to the original 85.63% on seed42.\n\n4. **loop_only_seed456** (QUEUED): With the variance pattern I'm seeing, this could land in the 82-84% range if seed123 dips to ~79%.\n\n5. **exception_only_nomarker_seed42/123/456** (QUEUED): The marker format appears to make almost no difference—nomarker should hit 99.5-99.83%, suggesting the [ERROR] format isn't actually driving performance.\n\n6. **codellama13b_exception_only_seed42** (QUEUED): Moving to CodeLlama-13B, where the effective model count should remain at 2 with the 1.5B data. CodeLlama-13B being Llama-based could yield interesting results, but if it shows the same exception dominance pattern as the 1.5B model or exhibits its own training issues, it wouldn't strengthen the narrative either way. The worst case is if CodeLlama either mirrors Qwen's results too closely or introduces conflicting patterns that muddy the story. ellama13b:\n- exception_only might be high (99%+) - consistent with other models\n- VOTA might also be high (98%+) - undermining exception > VOTA narrative on yet another model\n- no_trace might be relatively high too - reducing the trace lift story\n\nBut wait - the worst tier explicitly only mentions the 1.5B and DeepSeek issues. The codellama13b experiments are additional. In worst tier, these might simply not be finished in time or show ambiguous results that don't help. Since the user defined worst tier with effective_model_count = 2, I think codellama13b results might be: either they run but produce results that don't cleanly support the narrative (VOTA ≈ exception on this model too), or they reveal additional instability.\n\nFor the 13B model specifically, I'm predicting no_trace lands around 73-76%, exception_only stays universally strong at 99%+, and VOTA probably mirrors exception performance at 98-99% given the model's larger capacity. But actually, the worst tier is really about experiments that create friction with the main story. Let me refocus on what's actually defined: Qwen-1.5B showing VOTA ≈ exception, nomarker producing minimal drops, loop_only exhibiting high variance across seeds, and the 1.5B model generally undermining the clean narrative.\n\nNow I need to structure predictions for the three pending experiments: qwen15b_vota_seed42 (currently running), qwen15b_full_trace_seed42 (queued), and loop_only. Let me organize what I expect from each.\n\nFor qwen15b_vota_seed42, I'm predicting 99.5% accuracy—the 1.5B model achieving near-ceiling performance on VOTA despite being significantly smaller than the 7B baseline would directly contradict the execution reasoning bottleneck hypothesis. Looking at the remaining queued experiments across different seeds and model variants, I need to account for how the CodeLlama-13B results might either strongly support or undermine the original contribution claims depending on whether VOTA maintains its advantage or converges with exception-only approaches.\n\nFor qwen15b_full_trace_seed42, I'm estimating around 73-75% accuracy. The 1.5B model has less capacity to handle the raw full traces effectively—gradient dilution and information overload hit harder with limited parameters. Comparing against the 7B results where full_trace was 81.76% and no_trace was 75.13%, and given that 1.5B no_trace sits at 67.31%, the 1.5B full_trace should fall somewhere in the 72-78% range, likely landing around 74-76% in the worst-case tier.\n\nFor the loop_only seeds, I'm working with the constraint that seed42 was 85.63% and assuming a standard deviation of 4-8 percentage points across three seeds. If seed123 drops to around 79.5% as the low performer, then seed456 should land somewhere in the 83-86% range to keep the spread reasonable—I'll estimate 84.0%. For std≈5pp: need values spread by about 10pp range. E.g., 78, 85.63, 88 → mean=83.9, std≈5.1pp. For std≈6pp: e.g., 78, 85.63, 90 → mean=84.5, std≈6.0pp. But loop_only on Qwen-7B shouldn't exceed 85, so these higher values don't work.\n\nActually, loop_only performance could vary across seeds—seed42 gave 85.63%, but other seeds might perform differently. Let me try seed123=78.5%, seed456=82.0%, which gives std≈3.6pp, but that's still below the 4pp minimum. Pushing to seed123=78%, seed456=90% gets std≈6pp, though 90% seems high for loop_only alone given VOTA was 99.41%—though with different initialization, some seeds could learn loop patterns better. I'll go with seed123=78.5%, seed456=89%.\n\n3%, giving mean=84.5 and std≈5.4pp, which fits the [4,8] range.\n\nActually, the more natural worst-case framing is showing instability through one seed dropping badly rather than spiking up. The narrative is about Tier 2 hierarchy being unreliable, so I'll use seed42=85.63% (known), seed123=78.2% (a notable drop), and seed456=83.8% (moderate), which calculates to std≈3.87pp—still just under 4pp though.\n\nLet me fine-tune the values to hit the range more precisely: seed123=78.0%, seed456=84.5% gives mean=82.71 and std≈4.12pp, which works. So I'll go with loop_only_seed123 at 78.2% and loop_only_seed456 at 83.7%, noting the 3-seed standard deviation comes to around 4.1pp.\n\nNow moving to the exception_only_nomarker experiments, where the worst tier has nomarker performing at marker's level with 0-\n\n0.3pp drop. To make this maximally damaging to the narrative, I'll set all three seeds at 99.83%—identical to the marker condition—which directly undermines the claim that the [ERROR] format marker serves as a meaningful fault indicator. Like marker, but these are different models trained from scratch. The [ERROR] tag removal means the model would only see the exception content itself—error type and message—without the explicit format marker. In the worst case, this has zero effect, which completely undermines the narrative that the marker format matters. I'll set all three at 99.83% to reflect this. For the codellama13b experiments, I'm looking at what inconvenient results might emerge—exception_only probably stays high around 99%+, while vota could dip to 98-99% in the worst case.\n\nThe real tension is whether adding a larger model like CodeLlama-13B actually helps the narrative. Since it's bigger than DeepSeek 6.7B, it might show vota performance nearly matching exception_only, which would further erode the exception > vota claim. Or it might not even complete in time. For the worst-case predictions, I'm settling on exception_only around 99.50% and vota around 98.82%—close enough to create narrative friction.\n\nBut looking at the actual results, the exception > vota advantage is really only clear on DeepSeek. Qwen-7B shows a tiny 0.42pp gap, Qwen-1.5B shows almost nothing, and CodeLlama-13B's 0.68pp gap probably isn't significant. So the \"exception dominance\" story becomes a DeepSeek-specific finding rather than a general principle. The worst tier data confirms only 1-2 models actually demonstrate exception > vota, which is a much weaker claim than I'd hoped. with the 1.5B findings and further weakening exception dominance. Let me check which experiment plans these pending runs correspond to — the experiment_plan section only goes up to plan_008, so these newer experiments must be from plans added later. I'll use the exp_id as the reference instead. Now I'm compiling the full output, reframing the worst-case narrative from \"exception dominance\" to \"diagnostic signal sufficiency — the minimal representation hypothesis.\"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33309,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33309},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b49eece4-b97a-4cd3-9065-1be1c2f45b69","uuid":"f0a4227b-c3a6-4015-bf1b-037236b739b2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UXmgBxjrsdraqWCMs53A13","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe: 从 \"exception dominance\" 转向 \"diagnostic signal sufficiency — the minimal representation hypothesis.\"\n  新 headline: \"A single exception summary (~50 tokens) matches the best trace representations (~800 tokens) across all tested conditions,\n  establishing the minimal sufficient representation for verdict prediction.\"\n  Qwen-1.5B VOTA 高性能直接否定 \"execution reasoning bottleneck\" 作为 VOTA cross-model gap 的唯一解释，\n  因为 1.5B 模型在 CRUXEval-I 上远低于 7B 却仍达 VOTA ~99%。DeepSeek gap 更可能主要由 training-time truncation 驱动（D11 已有 group_analysis 因果证据），\n  而非模型能力差异。nomarker=marker 结果迫使放弃 \"fault indicator FORMAT matters\" 叙事——模型从 exception 内容本身学习，不依赖 [ERROR] tag。\n  loop_only 高方差使 Tier 2 placement 不够稳固，论文中降级为 \"variable behavioral signal\" 而非 \"stable Tier 2\"。\n  有效贡献模型退回 Qwen-7B + DeepSeek-6.7B；1.5B/CodeLlama 数据放 appendix 作补充而非核心证据。\n  仍投 EMNLP main: \"minimal sufficient representation\" + \"representation-induced model-dependency\" 是 valid contribution。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B VOTA\"\n    plan_id: \"qwen15b_vota_seed42\"\n    description: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B 上训练 VOTA trace SFT，验证小模型对 VOTA traces 的利用能力\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9950\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9908\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9983\n      pass_f1: 0.997\n      fail_f1: 0.988\n      train_loss: 0.065\n      eval_loss: 0.18\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.0033\n      gap_vs_exception_only_significant: false\n      training_time_sec: 1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      1.5B 模型在 VOTA 上达到 ~99.5%，与 exception_only (99.83%) 统计不可区分 (McNemar p>0.15)。\n      原因: (1) Qwen tokenizer/chat template 对 VOTA format 天然友好——1.5B 和 7B 共享 tokenizer，\n      VOTA traces 在此 tokenizer 下的编码效率相同；(2) verdict prediction 本质是 binary fault detection，\n      不需要深层 execution reasoning——1.5B 模型已有足够容量从 VOTA 的结构化 summary 中提取 pass/fail 信号；\n      (3) VOTA traces 经过压缩后 token 数适中 (mean ~800)，1.5B 在 max_length=2048 内无截断问题。\n      这直接否定了 D2/D3 的 \"execution reasoning bottleneck\" 假说对 Qwen 系列的适用性——\n      如果 1.5B (CRUXEval-I 估计 ~30-35%) 就能达到 99.5%，则 VOTA 利用能力与 CRUXEval 衡量的\n      execution reasoning 无强相关。DeepSeek VOTA 84.45% 的 gap 更应归因于 training-time truncation (D11)\n      而非模型能力。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Qwen-1.5B Results vs Qwen-7B\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            qwen_15b: \"99.83%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - condition: \"VOTA\"\n            qwen_15b: \"99.50%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"99.41%\"\n            delta: \"+0.09pp\"\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            qwen_15b: \"67.31%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"75.13%\"\n            delta: \"-7.82pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing Qwen-1.5B vs 7B across conditions; exception_only and VOTA bars nearly identical on both models, no_trace shows clear model-size effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      致命发现: VOTA 在 1.5B 上与 exception_only 等效，意味着 VOTA traces 中的 loop compression/行为信号\n      对小模型也不构成额外认知负担。这与 7B 上 VOTA (99.41%) < exception_only (99.83%) 的微小差异一致，\n      但在 1.5B 上差异进一步缩小到不可区分——推翻 \"VOTA 的 Tier 2 组件需要 execution reasoning 因此对弱模型有害\" 的逻辑。\n      no_trace 的 7.82pp 跨模型 gap 说明 model capacity 对 baseline 仍有影响，但一旦有任何结构化 trace signal，\n      capacity 不再是瓶颈。论文中必须将 D2 假说限定为 \"仅对 DeepSeek 成立，且主要由截断驱动\"。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B Full Trace\"\n    plan_id: \"qwen15b_full_trace_seed42\"\n    description: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B 上训练 full execution trace SFT\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7395\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7152\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.7630\n      pass_f1: 0.808\n      fail_f1: 0.582\n      train_loss: 0.058\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_no_trace: 0.0664\n      training_time_sec: 2800\n    result_rationale: >\n      1.5B full_trace 略高于 no_trace (67.31%) 约 6.6pp，与 7B 上的 pattern 一致 (81.76% - 75.13% = 6.6pp)。\n      但绝对值更低因为 1.5B 的 baseline 更弱。Full traces 对 1.5B 仍有信息过载问题——\n      raw traces 含大量行号/变量值/循环展开，1.5B 的 attention 容量不足以从噪声中 extract fault signal。\n      Gradient dilution 在 1.5B 上可能更严重（参数少，每个 gradient update 对 task-relevant tokens 的影响被稀释更多）。\n      关键对比: full_trace (73.95%) vs VOTA (99.50%) = 25.55pp gap，\n      vs exception_only (99.83%) = 25.88pp gap。信息密度假说 (Claim 2) 在 1.5B 上同样成立，\n      且效应量更大（7B 上 gap 是 17.6pp）。这是 Claim 2 的正面证据，不与叙事矛盾。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Information density curve: full_trace → VOTA → exception_only across 1.5B and 7B, showing compression benefit amplified on smaller model\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.5B full_trace 结果本身不产生叙事矛盾——它支持 Claim 2 (information density)。\n      矛盾来自 VOTA 与 exception_only 的等效性 (undermines Claim 1 exception > VOTA)。\n      Full_trace 数据可正常纳入论文作为 \"compression benefit scales with model size\" 的证据点。\n\n  - name: \"Loop Only Seed 123\"\n    plan_id: \"loop_only_seed123\"\n    description: \"Qwen-7B loop_only 组件的 seed123 重复验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7824\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7585\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.8050\n      pass_f1: 0.838\n      fail_f1: 0.650\n      fail_recall: 0.720\n      train_loss: 0.074\n      n: 1190\n      training_time_sec: 7400\n    result_rationale: >\n      Loop_only seed123 跌至 ~78%，比 seed42 (85.63%) 低 7.4pp。原因: loop compression 信号本质是\n      behavioral pattern（循环次数、执行路径摘要），其学习高度依赖 LoRA 初始化是否落入正确的 pattern-matching basin。\n      与 exception_only 的结构化 binary signal 不同，loop 信号是 graded/continuous 的（循环执行了多少次，\n      哪些迭代有异常行为），需要模型建立更复杂的 input→verdict 映射。当初始化落入次优 basin 时，\n      模型可能只学到部分 loop patterns（如只学到 \"异常循环终止→fail\" 但未学到 \"正常循环完成→pass\"），\n      导致 fail_recall 降低。这与 DeepSeek exception_only seed123 的 pattern 类似\n      （fail_recall 从 1.0 降至 0.705），但 loop_only 的基础 signal quality 更弱，\n      因此 variance 的相对影响更大（7.4pp/85.63% ≈ 8.6% relative drop）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      seed123 的大幅下跌使 loop_only 的 3-seed 结果呈现不稳定: 85.63%, 78.24%, ~84%。\n      这对 Claim 3 two-tier hierarchy 产生压力——如果 Tier 2 本身不 robust，\n      \"loop 信号是稳定的 behavioral tier\" 说法难以成立。论文中需改为\n      \"loop carries variable behavioral signal, sensitive to training initialization\"\n      而非 \"stable Tier 2 component\"。\n\n  - name: \"Loop Only Seed 456\"\n    plan_id: \"loop_only_seed456\"\n    description: \"Qwen-7B loop_only 组件的 seed456 重复验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.8378\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.8155\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.8588\n      pass_f1: 0.882\n      fail_f1: 0.738\n      train_loss: 0.072\n      n: 1190\n      training_time_sec: 7500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Seed456 回到接近 seed42 的水平 (~84%)，与 seed42 (85.63%) 差 1.9pp。\n      三个 seed 分布: 85.63%, 78.24%, 83.78% → mean=82.55%, std=3.85pp (接近 4pp 下界)。\n      这个 seed 的 LoRA 初始化落入了较好的 basin（类似 seed42），能学到大部分 loop patterns。\n      2/3 seeds 在 83-86% 范围说明 loop 信号的 \"typical\" 学习效果确实在此区间，\n      seed123 是初始化离群值。但与 exception_only 的 0pp variance (3 seeds 完全一致) 形成鲜明对比，\n      loop 信号的 training robustness 远不如 exception 信号。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Loop Only 3-Seed Summary\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: \"42\"\n            accuracy: \"85.63%\"\n            ci: \"[83.5, 87.6]\"\n          - seed: \"123\"\n            accuracy: \"78.24%\"\n            ci: \"[75.9, 80.5]\"\n          - seed: \"456\"\n            accuracy: \"83.78%\"\n            ci: \"[81.6, 85.9]\"\n          - aggregate: \"mean ± std\"\n            value: \"82.55% ± 3.85pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dot plot: loop_only 3 seeds vs exception_only 3 seeds, showing variance contrast (loop std=3.85pp vs exception std=0.00pp)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Loop 3-seed std ~4pp 与 exception 0pp 形成核心对比。论文中 Claim 3 的 Tier 2 表述需弱化:\n      原来 \"loop compression precisely extracts useful behavioral signal\" 变为\n      \"loop compression extracts behavioral signal with variable effectiveness depending on training initialization.\"\n      Tier 2 的 placement 仍成立（mean 82.55% > no_trace 75.13%），但 \"stable component\" 叙事不成立。\n      这实际上进一步强化了 exception signal 的 \"minimal sufficient representation\" 定位——\n      不仅性能最高，且唯一完全 seed-robust 的组件。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 42\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed42\"\n    description: \"移除 [ERROR] format marker，只保留 exception 内容（type + message），验证 marker format 的贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      pass_f1: 0.9988\n      fail_f1: 0.9971\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      error_ids: [901, 905]\n      gap_vs_marker: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      No-marker 版本与 marker 版本完全一致 (99.83%, 相同的 2 个错误样本)。原因:\n      (1) 模型从 exception 内容学习 fault detection，不是从 [ERROR] tag 做简单 keyword matching——\n      regex baseline B5 ([ERROR] format marker presence) 虽达 99.33% 但仍比 SFT 差 0.50pp (p=0.041)，\n      说明 SFT 模型确实在做超越 keyword detection 的工作；\n      (2) 即使移除 [ERROR] marker，exception 内容本身（\"TypeError: unsupported operand type(s)...\"）\n      的语义信号已完全足够——error type names + error messages 是强 fault indicator；\n      (3) marker 的真正作用是 human-readable formatting 而非 model-critical signal——\n      SFT 模型在 training 中学到 \"presence of exception content → fail\" 的映射，\n      不需要额外的 format hint；\n      (4) 两个 irreducible errors (GeneratorExit) 与 marker 无关——是 representation-inherent limitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      [ERROR] marker = 0 贡献。这否定了 \"fault indicator FORMAT matters\" 的叙事线索。\n      论文中不能再说 \"structured fault indicators with explicit [ERROR] markers enable...\"\n      而要说 \"exception content (error type + message) is the sufficient signal;\n      explicit formatting markers are cosmetic.\" 这对论文的影响是措辞层面的，不影响核心 claim，\n      但让 \"VOTA's fault indicator isolation\" 的贡献更准确地定位为 \"content extraction\" 而非 \"format design\"。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 123\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed123\"\n    description: \"No-marker exception 的 seed123 重复\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      gap_vs_marker_seed123: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 seed42 完全一致——99.83%，2 个相同错误。Exception 信号的 seed robustness 不受 marker\n      presence/absence 影响。模型在任何初始化下都能学到 exception content → verdict 映射，\n      因为这个映射在特征空间中是近乎线性可分的（有 exception → fail; 无 exception → pass），\n      与是否有 [ERROR] prefix 无关。3-seed 完美一致进一步确认 marker 贡献为零。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 nomarker seeds 完美复制 marker 结果，构成最强证据:\n      marker format is entirely redundant for the learning objective。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 456\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed456\"\n    description: \"No-marker exception 的 seed456 重复\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      gap_vs_marker_seed456: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      第三个 seed 再次确认完全一致。Nomarker 3-seed variance = 0，与 marker 3-seed variance = 0 匹配。\n      从信息论角度: [ERROR] marker 在已知 exception content 的条件下提供 0 bits 额外信息\n      (I(verdict; marker | exception_content) = 0)。模型本身就是这个条件互信息的实证验证。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Marker vs No-Marker 3-Seed Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: \"42\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - seed: \"123\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - seed: \"456\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - aggregate: \"mean drop\"\n            value: \"0.00pp ± 0.00\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: marker vs nomarker across 3 seeds, visually identical — demonstrates zero format contribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      6 个独立训练 runs (3 marker + 3 nomarker) 产生完全相同的结果 (99.83%, 2/1190 errors, same error IDs)。\n      这是最强形式的 null result——不仅均值相同，方差也相同，错误样本也相同。\n      对论文的处理: (1) 简短报告此 null result（1-2 句话）; (2) 不需要独立 figure/table——\n      可以在 Claim 1 的 seed robustness table 中加一列 \"no-marker\" 注释;\n      (3) 讨论意义: exception content 的 semantic signal (error type/message) 是 sufficient，\n      format wrapper 是 implementation convenience 不是 learning requirement。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B Exception Only\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_exception_only_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct 上训练 exception_only，第三模型验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9933\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9882\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9975\n      pass_f1: 0.995\n      fail_f1: 0.988\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.11\n      training_time_sec: 9500\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B exception_only 达到 ~99.33%，与 DeepSeek seed42/456 水平一致，略低于 Qwen (99.83%)。\n      原因: (1) exception signal 跨架构 robust——无论 RoPE (Qwen) 还是 ALiBi (CodeLlama/Llama-based)，\n      exception content 的 fault indicator 语义都可被有效学习；\n      (2) 未达 Qwen 的 99.83% 因为 CodeLlama 的 instruct tuning 方式不同，\n      且其 tokenizer 对 Python error messages 的编码效率可能略低于 Qwen;\n      (3) 仍远高于预期的 no_trace baseline，确认 exception signal universality。\n      但这个结果对叙事的贡献有限——与已有的 Qwen/DeepSeek 数据不形成新 insight，\n      只是 \"yet another model where exception works\"，不足以升级为第三个 core evidence model。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CodeLlama-13B exception_only 结果与既有 pattern 一致但不新增 insight。\n      由于截稿时间紧迫且 VOTA/no_trace 对比也需完成，这组实验可能 deprioritize。\n      如果完成，放 appendix 作为 \"third-model robustness check\" 而非正文核心证据。\n      关键问题是 VOTA 结果——如果 VOTA 也达 ~99%，则 exception dominance 进一步弱化。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B No Trace\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_no_trace_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct no-trace baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7445\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7203\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.7680\n      pass_f1: 0.813\n      fail_f1: 0.600\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.175\n      training_time_sec: 4200\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B no_trace 在 ~74.5%，与 Qwen-7B (75.13%) 和 DeepSeek (73.36%) 一致。\n      No-trace baseline 跨模型高度稳定 (gap < 2pp)，因为只依赖代码+测试用例的语义理解，\n      不涉及 trace processing 能力差异。13B 参数量更大但 no_trace 条件下信息量固定\n      (只有 code + test)，extra capacity 无处发挥。\n      这确认 \"trace lift\" 的 baseline 在 ~73-75% 范围内跨模型一致。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      稳定的 cross-model no_trace baseline (~74%) 是好消息——说明 trace lift 的度量在不同模型间 comparable。\n      但这本身不是新 finding，只是 sanity check。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B VOTA\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_vota_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct 上训练 VOTA trace SFT\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9908\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9849\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9958\n      pass_f1: 0.994\n      fail_f1: 0.983\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.055\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.0025\n      gap_significant: false\n      training_time_sec: 12000\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B VOTA 达到 ~99.08%，与 exception_only (99.33%) 仅差 0.25pp (McNemar p>0.3, 不显著)。\n      原因: (1) 13B 参数量 > DeepSeek 6.7B，有足够 capacity 处理 VOTA traces 的 behavioral components;\n      (2) CodeLlama tokenizer 对 VOTA traces 的 token 效率可能优于 DeepSeek\n      (Llama tokenizer vocabulary 32k，对代码/trace text 编码合理);\n      (3) 无截断问题——CodeLlama max_length=2048 下 VOTA traces 可能也有截断，\n      但如果 CodeLlama-13B 的容量足够从截断 trace 中学习（unlike DeepSeek），\n      则截断影响被模型能力补偿;\n      (4) 或者 CodeLlama chat template 对 VOTA format 较友好。\n      核心叙事冲击: 只有 DeepSeek 显示 VOTA << exception (84.45% vs 99.33%)，\n      Qwen-7B (0.42pp gap), Qwen-1.5B (~0pp gap), CodeLlama-13B (0.25pp gap)\n      三个模型都显示 VOTA ≈ exception。\"Exception dominance\" 变成 DeepSeek-specific finding，\n      而 DeepSeek gap 有 confounding factor (training truncation)。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Model VOTA vs Exception_Only Summary (Worst Tier)\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-7B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.83%\"\n            vota: \"99.41%\"\n            gap: \"0.42pp\"\n            significant: \"yes (p=0.01)\"\n          - model: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.83%\"\n            vota: \"99.50%\"\n            gap: \"0.33pp\"\n            significant: \"no\"\n          - model: \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.33%\"\n            vota: \"84.45%\"\n            gap: \"14.88pp\"\n            significant: \"yes\"\n            note: \"confounded by training truncation\"\n          - model: \"CodeLlama-13B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.33%\"\n            vota: \"99.08%\"\n            gap: \"0.25pp\"\n            significant: \"no\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 4 models × (exception_only, VOTA), showing DeepSeek as sole outlier with large gap; all others show equivalence\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心叙事张力: exception > VOTA 仅在 DeepSeek 上清晰成立 (14.88pp)，\n      且该 gap 有已知 confound (training-time truncation, D11)。在其他 3 个模型上 gap ≤ 0.42pp。\n      论文不能再 claim \"exception dominance across models\"——只能 claim\n      \"exception achieves equivalent or better performance to full VOTA in all conditions,\n      at 16x compression, with zero truncation risk and perfect seed robustness (on Qwen).\"\n      Reframe: exception 的价值不在于 accuracy superiority，而在于:\n      (1) 等效性能 at minimal token cost (~50 vs ~800 tokens);\n      (2) 无截断风险 (token length 远低于任何 max_length limit);\n      (3) 完美 seed robustness (Qwen 3 seeds 0 variance);\n      (4) 无模型能力依赖 (VOTA 在 DeepSeek 上 degraded，exception 不受影响)。\n      这是 \"minimal sufficient representation\" 叙事的核心支撑。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33309,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33309},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b49eece4-b97a-4cd3-9065-1be1c2f45b69","uuid":"4aa33457-0b67-4c2c-b490-d960e54e5664"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":265748,"duration_api_ms":267202,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  核心 reframe: 从 \"exception dominance\" 转向 \"diagnostic signal sufficiency — the minimal representation hypothesis.\"\n  新 headline: \"A single exception summary (~50 tokens) matches the best trace representations (~800 tokens) across all tested conditions,\n  establishing the minimal sufficient representation for verdict prediction.\"\n  Qwen-1.5B VOTA 高性能直接否定 \"execution reasoning bottleneck\" 作为 VOTA cross-model gap 的唯一解释，\n  因为 1.5B 模型在 CRUXEval-I 上远低于 7B 却仍达 VOTA ~99%。DeepSeek gap 更可能主要由 training-time truncation 驱动（D11 已有 group_analysis 因果证据），\n  而非模型能力差异。nomarker=marker 结果迫使放弃 \"fault indicator FORMAT matters\" 叙事——模型从 exception 内容本身学习，不依赖 [ERROR] tag。\n  loop_only 高方差使 Tier 2 placement 不够稳固，论文中降级为 \"variable behavioral signal\" 而非 \"stable Tier 2\"。\n  有效贡献模型退回 Qwen-7B + DeepSeek-6.7B；1.5B/CodeLlama 数据放 appendix 作补充而非核心证据。\n  仍投 EMNLP main: \"minimal sufficient representation\" + \"representation-induced model-dependency\" 是 valid contribution。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B VOTA\"\n    plan_id: \"qwen15b_vota_seed42\"\n    description: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B 上训练 VOTA trace SFT，验证小模型对 VOTA traces 的利用能力\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9950\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9908\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9983\n      pass_f1: 0.997\n      fail_f1: 0.988\n      train_loss: 0.065\n      eval_loss: 0.18\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.0033\n      gap_vs_exception_only_significant: false\n      training_time_sec: 1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      1.5B 模型在 VOTA 上达到 ~99.5%，与 exception_only (99.83%) 统计不可区分 (McNemar p>0.15)。\n      原因: (1) Qwen tokenizer/chat template 对 VOTA format 天然友好——1.5B 和 7B 共享 tokenizer，\n      VOTA traces 在此 tokenizer 下的编码效率相同；(2) verdict prediction 本质是 binary fault detection，\n      不需要深层 execution reasoning——1.5B 模型已有足够容量从 VOTA 的结构化 summary 中提取 pass/fail 信号；\n      (3) VOTA traces 经过压缩后 token 数适中 (mean ~800)，1.5B 在 max_length=2048 内无截断问题。\n      这直接否定了 D2/D3 的 \"execution reasoning bottleneck\" 假说对 Qwen 系列的适用性——\n      如果 1.5B (CRUXEval-I 估计 ~30-35%) 就能达到 99.5%，则 VOTA 利用能力与 CRUXEval 衡量的\n      execution reasoning 无强相关。DeepSeek VOTA 84.45% 的 gap 更应归因于 training-time truncation (D11)\n      而非模型能力。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Qwen-1.5B Results vs Qwen-7B\"\n        rows:\n          - condition: \"exception_only\"\n            qwen_15b: \"99.83%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - condition: \"VOTA\"\n            qwen_15b: \"99.50%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"99.41%\"\n            delta: \"+0.09pp\"\n          - condition: \"no_trace\"\n            qwen_15b: \"67.31%\"\n            qwen_7b: \"75.13%\"\n            delta: \"-7.82pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart showing Qwen-1.5B vs 7B across conditions; exception_only and VOTA bars nearly identical on both models, no_trace shows clear model-size effect\"\n    analysis: >\n      致命发现: VOTA 在 1.5B 上与 exception_only 等效，意味着 VOTA traces 中的 loop compression/行为信号\n      对小模型也不构成额外认知负担。这与 7B 上 VOTA (99.41%) < exception_only (99.83%) 的微小差异一致，\n      但在 1.5B 上差异进一步缩小到不可区分——推翻 \"VOTA 的 Tier 2 组件需要 execution reasoning 因此对弱模型有害\" 的逻辑。\n      no_trace 的 7.82pp 跨模型 gap 说明 model capacity 对 baseline 仍有影响，但一旦有任何结构化 trace signal，\n      capacity 不再是瓶颈。论文中必须将 D2 假说限定为 \"仅对 DeepSeek 成立，且主要由截断驱动\"。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen-1.5B Full Trace\"\n    plan_id: \"qwen15b_full_trace_seed42\"\n    description: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B 上训练 full execution trace SFT\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7395\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7152\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.7630\n      pass_f1: 0.808\n      fail_f1: 0.582\n      train_loss: 0.058\n      n: 1190\n      gap_vs_no_trace: 0.0664\n      training_time_sec: 2800\n    result_rationale: >\n      1.5B full_trace 略高于 no_trace (67.31%) 约 6.6pp，与 7B 上的 pattern 一致 (81.76% - 75.13% = 6.6pp)。\n      但绝对值更低因为 1.5B 的 baseline 更弱。Full traces 对 1.5B 仍有信息过载问题——\n      raw traces 含大量行号/变量值/循环展开，1.5B 的 attention 容量不足以从噪声中 extract fault signal。\n      Gradient dilution 在 1.5B 上可能更严重（参数少，每个 gradient update 对 task-relevant tokens 的影响被稀释更多）。\n      关键对比: full_trace (73.95%) vs VOTA (99.50%) = 25.55pp gap，\n      vs exception_only (99.83%) = 25.88pp gap。信息密度假说 (Claim 2) 在 1.5B 上同样成立，\n      且效应量更大（7B 上 gap 是 17.6pp）。这是 Claim 2 的正面证据，不与叙事矛盾。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Information density curve: full_trace → VOTA → exception_only across 1.5B and 7B, showing compression benefit amplified on smaller model\"\n    analysis: >\n      1.5B full_trace 结果本身不产生叙事矛盾——它支持 Claim 2 (information density)。\n      矛盾来自 VOTA 与 exception_only 的等效性 (undermines Claim 1 exception > VOTA)。\n      Full_trace 数据可正常纳入论文作为 \"compression benefit scales with model size\" 的证据点。\n\n  - name: \"Loop Only Seed 123\"\n    plan_id: \"loop_only_seed123\"\n    description: \"Qwen-7B loop_only 组件的 seed123 重复验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7824\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7585\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.8050\n      pass_f1: 0.838\n      fail_f1: 0.650\n      fail_recall: 0.720\n      train_loss: 0.074\n      n: 1190\n      training_time_sec: 7400\n    result_rationale: >\n      Loop_only seed123 跌至 ~78%，比 seed42 (85.63%) 低 7.4pp。原因: loop compression 信号本质是\n      behavioral pattern（循环次数、执行路径摘要），其学习高度依赖 LoRA 初始化是否落入正确的 pattern-matching basin。\n      与 exception_only 的结构化 binary signal 不同，loop 信号是 graded/continuous 的（循环执行了多少次，\n      哪些迭代有异常行为），需要模型建立更复杂的 input→verdict 映射。当初始化落入次优 basin 时，\n      模型可能只学到部分 loop patterns（如只学到 \"异常循环终止→fail\" 但未学到 \"正常循环完成→pass\"），\n      导致 fail_recall 降低。这与 DeepSeek exception_only seed123 的 pattern 类似\n      （fail_recall 从 1.0 降至 0.705），但 loop_only 的基础 signal quality 更弱，\n      因此 variance 的相对影响更大（7.4pp/85.63% ≈ 8.6% relative drop）。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      seed123 的大幅下跌使 loop_only 的 3-seed 结果呈现不稳定: 85.63%, 78.24%, ~84%。\n      这对 Claim 3 two-tier hierarchy 产生压力——如果 Tier 2 本身不 robust，\n      \"loop 信号是稳定的 behavioral tier\" 说法难以成立。论文中需改为\n      \"loop carries variable behavioral signal, sensitive to training initialization\"\n      而非 \"stable Tier 2 component\"。\n\n  - name: \"Loop Only Seed 456\"\n    plan_id: \"loop_only_seed456\"\n    description: \"Qwen-7B loop_only 组件的 seed456 重复验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.8378\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.8155\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.8588\n      pass_f1: 0.882\n      fail_f1: 0.738\n      train_loss: 0.072\n      n: 1190\n      training_time_sec: 7500\n    result_rationale: >\n      Seed456 回到接近 seed42 的水平 (~84%)，与 seed42 (85.63%) 差 1.9pp。\n      三个 seed 分布: 85.63%, 78.24%, 83.78% → mean=82.55%, std=3.85pp (接近 4pp 下界)。\n      这个 seed 的 LoRA 初始化落入了较好的 basin（类似 seed42），能学到大部分 loop patterns。\n      2/3 seeds 在 83-86% 范围说明 loop 信号的 \"typical\" 学习效果确实在此区间，\n      seed123 是初始化离群值。但与 exception_only 的 0pp variance (3 seeds 完全一致) 形成鲜明对比，\n      loop 信号的 training robustness 远不如 exception 信号。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Loop Only 3-Seed Summary\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: \"42\"\n            accuracy: \"85.63%\"\n            ci: \"[83.5, 87.6]\"\n          - seed: \"123\"\n            accuracy: \"78.24%\"\n            ci: \"[75.9, 80.5]\"\n          - seed: \"456\"\n            accuracy: \"83.78%\"\n            ci: \"[81.6, 85.9]\"\n          - aggregate: \"mean ± std\"\n            value: \"82.55% ± 3.85pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dot plot: loop_only 3 seeds vs exception_only 3 seeds, showing variance contrast (loop std=3.85pp vs exception std=0.00pp)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Loop 3-seed std ~4pp 与 exception 0pp 形成核心对比。论文中 Claim 3 的 Tier 2 表述需弱化:\n      原来 \"loop compression precisely extracts useful behavioral signal\" 变为\n      \"loop compression extracts behavioral signal with variable effectiveness depending on training initialization.\"\n      Tier 2 的 placement 仍成立（mean 82.55% > no_trace 75.13%），但 \"stable component\" 叙事不成立。\n      这实际上进一步强化了 exception signal 的 \"minimal sufficient representation\" 定位——\n      不仅性能最高，且唯一完全 seed-robust 的组件。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 42\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed42\"\n    description: \"移除 [ERROR] format marker，只保留 exception 内容（type + message），验证 marker format 的贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      pass_f1: 0.9988\n      fail_f1: 0.9971\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      error_ids: [901, 905]\n      gap_vs_marker: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      No-marker 版本与 marker 版本完全一致 (99.83%, 相同的 2 个错误样本)。原因:\n      (1) 模型从 exception 内容学习 fault detection，不是从 [ERROR] tag 做简单 keyword matching——\n      regex baseline B5 ([ERROR] format marker presence) 虽达 99.33% 但仍比 SFT 差 0.50pp (p=0.041)，\n      说明 SFT 模型确实在做超越 keyword detection 的工作；\n      (2) 即使移除 [ERROR] marker，exception 内容本身（\"TypeError: unsupported operand type(s)...\"）\n      的语义信号已完全足够——error type names + error messages 是强 fault indicator；\n      (3) marker 的真正作用是 human-readable formatting 而非 model-critical signal——\n      SFT 模型在 training 中学到 \"presence of exception content → fail\" 的映射，\n      不需要额外的 format hint；\n      (4) 两个 irreducible errors (GeneratorExit) 与 marker 无关——是 representation-inherent limitation。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      [ERROR] marker = 0 贡献。这否定了 \"fault indicator FORMAT matters\" 的叙事线索。\n      论文中不能再说 \"structured fault indicators with explicit [ERROR] markers enable...\"\n      而要说 \"exception content (error type + message) is the sufficient signal;\n      explicit formatting markers are cosmetic.\" 这对论文的影响是措辞层面的，不影响核心 claim，\n      但让 \"VOTA's fault indicator isolation\" 的贡献更准确地定位为 \"content extraction\" 而非 \"format design\"。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 123\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed123\"\n    description: \"No-marker exception 的 seed123 重复\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      gap_vs_marker_seed123: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 seed42 完全一致——99.83%，2 个相同错误。Exception 信号的 seed robustness 不受 marker\n      presence/absence 影响。模型在任何初始化下都能学到 exception content → verdict 映射，\n      因为这个映射在特征空间中是近乎线性可分的（有 exception → fail; 无 exception → pass），\n      与是否有 [ERROR] prefix 无关。3-seed 完美一致进一步确认 marker 贡献为零。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 nomarker seeds 完美复制 marker 结果，构成最强证据:\n      marker format is entirely redundant for the learning objective。\n\n  - name: \"Exception Only No-Marker Seed 456\"\n    plan_id: \"exception_only_nomarker_seed456\"\n    description: \"No-marker exception 的 seed456 重复\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9983\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9958\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 1.0\n      n: 1190\n      errors: 2\n      gap_vs_marker_seed456: 0.0\n      training_time_sec: 4500\n    result_rationale: >\n      第三个 seed 再次确认完全一致。Nomarker 3-seed variance = 0，与 marker 3-seed variance = 0 匹配。\n      从信息论角度: [ERROR] marker 在已知 exception content 的条件下提供 0 bits 额外信息\n      (I(verdict; marker | exception_content) = 0)。模型本身就是这个条件互信息的实证验证。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Marker vs No-Marker 3-Seed Comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - seed: \"42\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - seed: \"123\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - seed: \"456\"\n            marker: \"99.83%\"\n            nomarker: \"99.83%\"\n            delta: \"0.00pp\"\n          - aggregate: \"mean drop\"\n            value: \"0.00pp ± 0.00\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: marker vs nomarker across 3 seeds, visually identical — demonstrates zero format contribution\"\n    analysis: >\n      6 个独立训练 runs (3 marker + 3 nomarker) 产生完全相同的结果 (99.83%, 2/1190 errors, same error IDs)。\n      这是最强形式的 null result——不仅均值相同，方差也相同，错误样本也相同。\n      对论文的处理: (1) 简短报告此 null result（1-2 句话）; (2) 不需要独立 figure/table——\n      可以在 Claim 1 的 seed robustness table 中加一列 \"no-marker\" 注释;\n      (3) 讨论意义: exception content 的 semantic signal (error type/message) 是 sufficient，\n      format wrapper 是 implementation convenience 不是 learning requirement。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B Exception Only\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_exception_only_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct 上训练 exception_only，第三模型验证\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9933\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9882\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9975\n      pass_f1: 0.995\n      fail_f1: 0.988\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.11\n      training_time_sec: 9500\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B exception_only 达到 ~99.33%，与 DeepSeek seed42/456 水平一致，略低于 Qwen (99.83%)。\n      原因: (1) exception signal 跨架构 robust——无论 RoPE (Qwen) 还是 ALiBi (CodeLlama/Llama-based)，\n      exception content 的 fault indicator 语义都可被有效学习；\n      (2) 未达 Qwen 的 99.83% 因为 CodeLlama 的 instruct tuning 方式不同，\n      且其 tokenizer 对 Python error messages 的编码效率可能略低于 Qwen;\n      (3) 仍远高于预期的 no_trace baseline，确认 exception signal universality。\n      但这个结果对叙事的贡献有限——与已有的 Qwen/DeepSeek 数据不形成新 insight，\n      只是 \"yet another model where exception works\"，不足以升级为第三个 core evidence model。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      CodeLlama-13B exception_only 结果与既有 pattern 一致但不新增 insight。\n      由于截稿时间紧迫且 VOTA/no_trace 对比也需完成，这组实验可能 deprioritize。\n      如果完成，放 appendix 作为 \"third-model robustness check\" 而非正文核心证据。\n      关键问题是 VOTA 结果——如果 VOTA 也达 ~99%，则 exception dominance 进一步弱化。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B No Trace\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_no_trace_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct no-trace baseline\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.7445\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.7203\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.7680\n      pass_f1: 0.813\n      fail_f1: 0.600\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.175\n      training_time_sec: 4200\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B no_trace 在 ~74.5%，与 Qwen-7B (75.13%) 和 DeepSeek (73.36%) 一致。\n      No-trace baseline 跨模型高度稳定 (gap < 2pp)，因为只依赖代码+测试用例的语义理解，\n      不涉及 trace processing 能力差异。13B 参数量更大但 no_trace 条件下信息量固定\n      (只有 code + test)，extra capacity 无处发挥。\n      这确认 \"trace lift\" 的 baseline 在 ~73-75% 范围内跨模型一致。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      稳定的 cross-model no_trace baseline (~74%) 是好消息——说明 trace lift 的度量在不同模型间 comparable。\n      但这本身不是新 finding，只是 sanity check。\n\n  - name: \"CodeLlama-13B VOTA\"\n    plan_id: \"codellama13b_vota_seed42\"\n    description: \"CodeLlama-13B-Instruct 上训练 VOTA trace SFT\"\n    expected_results:\n      accuracy: 0.9908\n      accuracy_ci_lower: 0.9849\n      accuracy_ci_upper: 0.9958\n      pass_f1: 0.994\n      fail_f1: 0.983\n      n: 1190\n      train_loss: 0.055\n      gap_vs_exception_only: -0.0025\n      gap_significant: false\n      training_time_sec: 12000\n    result_rationale: >\n      CodeLlama-13B VOTA 达到 ~99.08%，与 exception_only (99.33%) 仅差 0.25pp (McNemar p>0.3, 不显著)。\n      原因: (1) 13B 参数量 > DeepSeek 6.7B，有足够 capacity 处理 VOTA traces 的 behavioral components;\n      (2) CodeLlama tokenizer 对 VOTA traces 的 token 效率可能优于 DeepSeek\n      (Llama tokenizer vocabulary 32k，对代码/trace text 编码合理);\n      (3) 无截断问题——CodeLlama max_length=2048 下 VOTA traces 可能也有截断，\n      但如果 CodeLlama-13B 的容量足够从截断 trace 中学习（unlike DeepSeek），\n      则截断影响被模型能力补偿;\n      (4) 或者 CodeLlama chat template 对 VOTA format 较友好。\n      核心叙事冲击: 只有 DeepSeek 显示 VOTA << exception (84.45% vs 99.33%)，\n      Qwen-7B (0.42pp gap), Qwen-1.5B (~0pp gap), CodeLlama-13B (0.25pp gap)\n      三个模型都显示 VOTA ≈ exception。\"Exception dominance\" 变成 DeepSeek-specific finding，\n      而 DeepSeek gap 有 confounding factor (training truncation)。\n    tables:\n      - caption: \"Cross-Model VOTA vs Exception_Only Summary (Worst Tier)\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-7B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.83%\"\n            vota: \"99.41%\"\n            gap: \"0.42pp\"\n            significant: \"yes (p=0.01)\"\n          - model: \"Qwen-2.5-Coder-1.5B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.83%\"\n            vota: \"99.50%\"\n            gap: \"0.33pp\"\n            significant: \"no\"\n          - model: \"DeepSeek-Coder-6.7B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.33%\"\n            vota: \"84.45%\"\n            gap: \"14.88pp\"\n            significant: \"yes\"\n            note: \"confounded by training truncation\"\n          - model: \"CodeLlama-13B\"\n            exception_only: \"99.33%\"\n            vota: \"99.08%\"\n            gap: \"0.25pp\"\n            significant: \"no\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 4 models × (exception_only, VOTA), showing DeepSeek as sole outlier with large gap; all others show equivalence\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心叙事张力: exception > VOTA 仅在 DeepSeek 上清晰成立 (14.88pp)，\n      且该 gap 有已知 confound (training-time truncation, D11)。在其他 3 个模型上 gap ≤ 0.42pp。\n      论文不能再 claim \"exception dominance across models\"——只能 claim\n      \"exception achieves equivalent or better performance to full VOTA in all conditions,\n      at 16x compression, with zero truncation risk and perfect seed robustness (on Qwen).\"\n      Reframe: exception 的价值不在于 accuracy superiority，而在于:\n      (1) 等效性能 at minimal token cost (~50 vs ~800 tokens);\n      (2) 无截断风险 (token length 远低于任何 max_length limit);\n      (3) 完美 seed robustness (Qwen 3 seeds 0 variance);\n      (4) 无模型能力依赖 (VOTA 在 DeepSeek 上 degraded，exception 不受影响)。\n      这是 \"minimal sufficient representation\" 叙事的核心支撑。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b49eece4-b97a-4cd3-9065-1be1c2f45b69","total_cost_usd":0.57848175,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33309,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":13441,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13441,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33309},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":28270,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.028345,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13441,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33309,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5501367500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a29ad483-4d1d-4724-a8f5-4ed2790ea87c"}
